# Base system
base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
plymouth
amd-ucode
intel-ucode
sudo
nano
vim
networkmanager
openssh
reflector

# Partitioning / filesystem tools Calamares' partition/fstab/unpackfs modules
# need. btrfs-progs: root is Btrfs (see etc/calamares/modules/partition.conf)
# so holtos-btrfs-snapshot can take real read-only snapshots for the Limine
# "boot into a snapshot" menu entries — e2fsprogs stays too, only for
# whatever the live medium's own squashfs/overlay work still touches, root
# itself is no longer ext4.
arch-install-scripts
parted
gptfdisk
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
btrfs-progs
squashfs-tools
rsync
syslinux

# ZFS for the data pool (AUR, via the local repo — see pacman.conf)
zfs-dkms
zfs-utils
linux-headers

# Limine bootloader (installed onto the TARGET system by Calamares, not
# used for the live medium's own boot — see archiso/airootfs/etc/calamares).
# NOTE: deliberately NOT installing limine-mkinitcpio-hook — its pacman hook
# auto-deploys Limine to a FAT32 ESP on every kernel/initramfs update, which
# breaks the archiso build (no real ESP exists inside the build chroot) and
# is redundant with our own homelab-limine-install.sh anyway.
limine
limine-entry-tool

# KDE Plasma desktop
plasma-desktop
# HoltOS Glass type: Nunito (display/body) + JetBrains Mono (eyebrows,
# paths, numbers) — used by the installer QML/QSS, the SDDM theme, and the
# Plasma defaults. Both are in extra.
ttf-nunito
ttf-jetbrains-mono
sddm
konsole
dolphin
# Neon rebrand: GTK apps show their menus in the top menu bar
appmenu-gtk-module
plasma-nm
# System Settings > About this System (kinfocenter, reads /etc/os-release and
# etc/xdg/kcm-about-distrorc), Power Management profiles
# (power-profiles-daemon: performance / balanced / power saver in the
# battery widget and the Power KCM), and a task manager.
kinfocenter
power-profiles-daemon
# python-gobject: powerprofilesctl (the daemon's CLI) is a Python script
# importing gi.repository; without it the command tracebacks (seen live
# 2026-09-12, build 9). The Plasma applet talks D-Bus directly and does
# not need it, but the CLI is what scripts and support checks use.
python-gobject
plasma-systemmonitor
# System Settings pages a Plasma desktop is expected to have but that
# plasma-desktop alone does not pull in — found on the build 9 install
# (2026-09-12): System Settings > Display opened to "Could not find
# plugin kcm_kscreen", so there was NO resolution / refresh rate / scale /
# HDR / VRR page at all (libkscreen was there, the KCM package was not).
# kscreen: Display Configuration page + the kded module that applies it.
# plasma-pa: audio volume applet and Audio page (needs the pipewire stack
# already in the list). bluedevil: Bluetooth applet + page (remotes,
# headphones). kde-gtk-config: GTK apps follow the HoltOS theme.
# plasma-disks: SMART disk-health monitoring and warnings — a media
# server's disks are the whole point. sddm-kcm: Login Screen page.
# kwallet-pam: unlocks KWallet at login so Wi-Fi/Bluetooth secrets don't
# prompt. krdp: the Remote Desktop (RDP server) page, so the box can be
# driven headless from another machine.
kscreen
plasma-pa
bluedevil
kde-gtk-config
plasma-disks
# smartmontools: the smartd daemon behind the disk-health alerts
# (etc/smartd.conf -> holtos-disk-alert -> per-login notice). plasma-disks
# only pulls it in as a dependency; listed explicitly so enabling
# smartd.service in customize_airootfs.sh can never silently break.
smartmontools
sddm-kcm
kwallet-pam
krdp
# ...and the daemons behind two of those pages, also absent from build 9:
# pipewire-pulse + pipewire-alsa (pipewire and wireplumber were there, but
# nothing served the PulseAudio API plasma-pa and every desktop app use),
# bluez + bluez-utils (the Bluetooth daemon bluedevil talks to; enabled in
# customize_airootfs.sh).
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
bluez
bluez-utils
ark
print-manager
# The Den's own web UI (the-den.desktop opens http://127.0.0.1:8686) needs a
# browser; nothing else in this package list provides one.
falkon
# The Den v0.5.1+ depends on chromium (its built-in Cloudflare solver for
# public trackers, app/indexers/solver.py); build-vendor-apps refuses to
# vendor a release whose depends are missing from this list.
chromium

# Calamares installer (AUR, via the local repo). polkit provides pkexec,
# which the installer's desktop launcher uses to gain root.
calamares
polkit

# HoltOS updater (holtos-tray / holtos-update*): git for `ls-remote` tag
# lookups (metadata only, no clone), curl to download the release tarball
# and query the GitHub Releases API, jq to parse that API's JSON (release
# notes in update notifications), yad for the system-tray icon + menu,
# libnotify for the "update available" desktop notification. breeze-gtk:
# yad is a GTK3 app — without this it renders as plain light Adwaita,
# clashing with the rest of the dark/purple theme (see
# /etc/skel/.config/gtk-3.0/ for the dark+accent defaults).
git
curl
jq
yad
libnotify
# Updater: checkupdates (pacman-contrib; it needs fakeroot, only an
# optional dependency there) lists system updates without touching
# pacman's sync database; fwupd updates device firmware from LVFS.
pacman-contrib
fakeroot
fwupd
# HoltOS Apps: Flatpak for Flathub apps (the remote comes from
# /etc/flatpak/remotes.d), flatpak-kcm for per-app permissions in System
# Settings.
flatpak
flatpak-kcm
# TV remotes over HDMI-CEC: libcec (cec-client, and what Kodi and the
# Jellyfin and Plex players use to talk to the TV).
libcec
# AppImages: most still link the FUSE 2 library (libfuse.so.2), so without
# fuse2 they fail to start (many game launchers and tools ship this way).
fuse2
# On-screen keyboard for touch input (KWin's InputMethod in etc/xdg/kwinrc).
plasma-keyboard
# Controllers (AUR, in local-repo/): Xbox pads over Bluetooth, and udev
# rules so non-Steam controllers work without root.
xpadneo-dkms
game-devices-udev
breeze-gtk

# The Den (jamesyoungdahr-debug/the-den) — the movie/TV library manager
# HoltOS exists to run — and The Den Client (jamesyoungdahr-debug/
# the-den-client), its native KDE desktop app. Both are separately-
# maintained repos whose latest tagged release is baked into this image at
# build time (build-vendor-apps.sh → customize_airootfs.sh →
# `holtos-update-apply vendor`) and updated in place afterwards by the same
# code path from the tray. python: the-den's own venv + alembic migrations. pyside6/kirigami/qqc2-desktop-style: the client's
# runtime, no separate venv needed (it has no pip dependencies of its own).
# pyside6 is also what holtos-tray (the updater's tray icon) is built on
# now — see that script's own header for why (yad's tray mode is
# X11-only, doesn't work under Wayland at all). qt6-wayland: real crash
# found live-testing the Btrfs install — without it, PySide6's
# QSystemTrayIcon.isSystemTrayAvailable() straight-up segfaults under this
# session's Wayland (XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland), confirmed via
# coredumpctl info (SIGSEGV inside libQt6Widgets.so's
# QSystemTrayIcon::isSystemTrayAvailable, called from holtos-tray on both
# its autostart launch and a manual foreground run — not a one-off).
# qt6-wayland is Qt6's actual Wayland platform integration; PySide6 pulls
# in Qt6 itself but not this separate platform plugin package, so it was
# silently missing the whole time despite pyside6 nominally "supporting"
# Wayland.
# libtorrent-rasterbar: The Den >= v0.2.0 embeds its own torrent client on
# libtorrent's Python bindings, which come from this OS package (no PyPI
# wheel for the shipped CPython) — the-den's PKGBUILD depends on it and
# its venv is created with --system-site-packages to see it. Real outage
# 2026-09-11: the tray updater moved an install to v0.2.0 and the-den
# died with "No module named libtorrent" because this was missing.
# qt6-declarative: The Den Client >= v0.4.3 lists it in its PKGBUILD (QML
# engine + Qt Quick Controls it renders with); build-vendor-apps.sh refused
# to build the image without it (2026-09-12).
python
pyside6
qt6-wayland
# cifs-utils + nfs-utils: mount.cifs / mount.nfs for the Network Shares
# tool (holtos-shares GUI, holtos-share backend, systemd automount units).
cifs-utils
nfs-utils
qt6-declarative
libtorrent-rasterbar
kirigami
qqc2-desktop-style

# HoltOS Glass windows: Kvantum is the one Qt widget style that can make
# application windows translucent and ask KWin to blur behind them
# (usr/share/Kvantum/HoltOSGlass). Breeze cannot.
kvantum

# HoltOS Glass title bars: Klassy window decoration (AUR, in local-repo/ —
# see build-aur-packages.sh) can make the title bar translucent and blurred;
# Breeze cannot. Configured in etc/skel/.config/klassy/klassyrc.
holtos-window-decoration
holtos-glass-effect

# HoltOS's own full builds of KWin and plasma-workspace (Milestone 1 of docs/holtos-plasma-fork-plan.md) -- provides=()/conflicts=() in their PKGBUILDs replace the stock extra/ versions; no HoltOS customization in them yet, this just proves the build pipeline works.
holtos-kwin
holtos-plasma-workspace

# Hardware support that is safe on every machine (see
# usr/local/bin/homelab-detect-hardware.sh for the one that is not: NVIDIA).
# pciutils: lspci, which that script detects with. Mesa itself comes with
# Plasma; these add Vulkan for AMD/Intel and hardware video decode.
pciutils
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
intel-media-driver
libva-mesa-driver
# --- Gaming (docs/holtos-must-haves-and-plan.md 1.1 / 1.4) ---------------
# steam brings Proton; Proton GE is fetched from its GitHub releases by
# holtos-proton-ge. gamescope is the Game Mode compositor (1.2). lib32-*
# Vulkan drivers are what 32-bit games and Proton's Wine need on
# AMD/Intel (NVIDIA's lib32-nvidia-utils is staged with its driver and
# installed by homelab-detect-hardware.sh only when the card is there).
# gamemode + mangohud (and their lib32 halves) for the in-game
# performance daemon and overlay. zram-generator for compressed swap
# (etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf). xdg-desktop-portal-kde: Steam Big
# Picture's native file dialogs and screen-share/capture under Wayland go
# through the XDG desktop portal; plasma-desktop does not pull this in on
# its own, and without it Steam's file browser and screenshare portal
# requests silently fail (found 2026-09-13, not yet build-verified in the VM).
steam
gamescope
gamemode
lib32-gamemode
mangohud
lib32-mangohud
xdg-desktop-portal-kde
vulkan-icd-loader
lib32-vulkan-icd-loader
lib32-vulkan-radeon
lib32-vulkan-intel
lib32-mesa
zram-generator
# libva-utils (vainfo) and vulkan-tools (vulkaninfo): what
# homelab-detect-hardware.sh logs for AMD/Intel GPUs into hardware.log,
# and what a support check runs first on a real machine (Strix Halo).
libva-utils
vulkan-tools
